WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
I need 100 matte prints for an event in three days.
I want an AI to help buy them. But I still need control over the price
and terms I agree to, when permission ends, and whether payment completed.
The cheapest offer may miss the event. This is an illustrative buyer story.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:38.000
In separate actual model tests, explanations got prices and deadline
assumptions wrong. Advice cannot settle what I meant or authorize purchase.
An uncertain payment response needs a checkable answer before anyone pays again.
No purchase occurred in these model cases; the explanation stays unverified.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Vowrail starts with bounded permission stored outside the model's reasoning.
Here I allow at most USD 220 and two negotiation rounds.
Sellers receive public requirements, not my private ceiling.
This prototype keeps buyer review and approval explicit.
This is recorded local simulation, with no new provider calls.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The gateway enforces those bounds even when an adviser proposes something else.
Above-budget and invented offers cannot start checkout.
The gateway checks the round limit; a disabled button is only the interface.
The displayed policy checks are retained evidence, not a new operation.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:40.000
I compare the stored price, delivery estimate and expiry,
then choose the offer myself. Delivery and missing tax or refund terms
still need my review. Order creation, buyer approval and capture are separate.
The model explanation stays unverified. No new order is created here.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Permission has a lifetime. An expired quote cannot begin checkout,
and an expired mandate cannot authorize capture.
Previously completed payment status can still be checked.
This screen is a synthetic expiry replay, with no checkout or capture.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:25.000
In an earlier, separate PayPal Sandbox run, one USD 207 purchase completed.
Independent checks matched the stored amount, currency and reference.
Restart restored the completed receipt after expiry; recovery made no capture call.
This text summary omits private references. The synthetic seller was not the payee.
These were separate runs, not a new model-led purchase or transaction.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:45.000
The goal is to use AI help while keeping purchase permission explicit
and the outcome checkable. This local prototype demonstrates those controls,
not dependable model reasoning or guaranteed delivery.
The model cases and Sandbox purchase were separate runs.
This remains a private review, not a submitted or public video.
